      {
        "id": "lem-ip-tv-level-set-uniform-density-and-hausdorff",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Uniform density and Hausdorff convergence of TV level-set boundaries",
        "deps": [
          "def-ip-tv-level-set-representatives-and-boundaries",
          "def-ip-tv-variational-curvature",
          "def-ip-spatial-bv-and-distributional-tv",
          "def-ip-boundary-tv-conventions",
          "lem-ip-tv-dual-attainment-and-certificate-limit",
          "lem-ip-tv-vanishing-noise-primal-compactness",
          "lem-ip-bv-coarea-formula",
          "lem-ip-bv-test-field-characterization-and-lsc",
          "lem-ip-planar-isoperimetric-inequality-for-finite-perimeter-sets",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "lem-ip-tv-l2-coarea-formula",
          "lem-ip-neumann-bv-sobolev-poincare",
          "lem-ip-tv-l2-functional-properties",
          "def-ip-tv-functional-on-l2-distributional-variation",
          "thm-bolzano-weierstrass",
          "def-ip-tv-dual-source-certificate"
        ],
        "statement": "Under full-space, bounded Dirichlet, or bounded connected Neumann TV conventions, for α_n→0 and ||A*||||w_n||/α_n≤η, source-certified regularized level sets have the branch-specific variational-curvature and equality properties, uniform two-sided density bounds below the stated threshold, and a common bounded support in the full-plane branch. Whenever these level sets converge in measure, their canonical ambient boundaries converge in Hausdorff distance; bounded Dirichlet also assumes the global obstacle-curvature lower bound and Neumann uses the BV Sobolev–Poincaré constant CΩ.",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "José A. Iglesias, Gwenael Mercier, and Otmar Scherzer, A note on convergence of solutions of total variation regularized linear inverse problems, Lemmas 3–7 and §4, complete argument",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1711.06495"
